DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The llooggggeerr utility provides a shell command interface to the syslog(3)
     system log module.

     The following options are available:

     --44      Force llooggggeerr to use IPv4 addresses only.

     --66      Force llooggggeerr to use IPv6 addresses only.

     --AA      By default, llooggggeerr tries to send the message to only one address,
             even if the host has more than one A or AAAA record.  If this op‐
             tion is specified, llooggggeerr tries to send the message to all ad‐
             dresses.

     --ii      Log the process id of the logger process with each line.  This
             flag is ignored and the process id is always logged.  See also
             --tt.

     --ss      Log the message to standard error, as well as the system log.

     --ff _f_i_l_e
             Read the contents of the specified file into syslog.  This option
             is ignored when a message is also specified.

     --HH _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e
             Set the hostname in the header of the message to specified value.
             If not specified, host part of gethostname(3) will be used.

     --hh _h_o_s_t
             Send the message to the remote system _h_o_s_t instead of logging it
             locally.  Note that llooggggeerr currently supports AF_INET (IPv4),
             AF_INET6 (IPv6), and AF_LOCAL (Unix-domain socket) address fami‐
             lies.  The following address formats are valid in _h_o_s_t:

             AF_INET   192.168.2.1
             AF_INET6  2001:db8::1
             AF_LOCAL  _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_l_o_g

     --PP _p_o_r_t
             Send the message to the specified _p_o_r_t number on a remote system,
             which can be specified as a service name or as a decimal number.
             The default is “syslog”.  If an unknown service name is used,
             llooggggeerr prints a warning and falls back to port 514.

     --pp _p_r_i  Enter the message with the specified priority.  The priority may
             be specified numerically or as a facility.level pair.  For exam‐
             ple, “--pp local3.info” logs the message(s) as _i_n_f_ormational level
             in the _l_o_c_a_l_3 facility.  The default is “user.notice”.

     --SS _a_d_d_r:_p_o_r_t
             Specify source address and/or source port when using --hh option.
             The same address will be used for all of the remote addresses
             when --AA flag is enabled.  Note that a numeric IPv6 address in
             _a_d_d_r must be enclosed with “[” and “]”.

     --tt _t_a_g  Mark every line in the log with the specified _t_a_g rather than the
             default of current login name.  Use --tt _t_a_g_[_N_] to insert specific
             decimal process id instead of id of llooggggeerr.

     _m_e_s_s_a_g_e
             Write the message to log; if not specified, and the --ff flag is
             not provided, standard input is logged.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The llooggggeerr utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

